          "response": {
            "answer": "Le Tourin is a French garlic soup from the village of Le Fleix in Dordogne, and the recipe is 30 minutes total and serves 2. To make it, first brown the chopped garlic in olive oil in a frying pan. Then add the flour, mix well, and cook for a few minutes to remove the floury taste. Gradually stir in the water and cook for 10 minutes. Beat the egg white in a small bowl, gradually whisk in a ladleful of the soup to temper it, then stir the mixture back into the soup pot. Combine the egg yolk, pepper, and vinegar in a small bowl, temper the yolks with a ladleful of soup, then remove the soup from the heat and stir in the yolk mixture. Season to taste with salt. Place thin slices of bread in each soup bowl, pour the soup on top, and serve hot. The page notes you can optionally use an equal mixture of chopped onions and garlic. The ingredient list comes from the source page and may be incomplete.",
